# Secrets. The mnemonic and keystore password live here, so this must stay
# ignored: a committed .env is a committed key.
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Key material, under whatever name it was saved with.
*.keystore
mnemonic.txt
phrase.txt
wallet.json

# The record of who was paid. It is per-run operational state, and it names
# every recipient of every airdrop, so it does not belong in the history.
*.jsonl
airdrop-journal*

# Scan logs. Each one carries the full address list of everybody who
# transacted in a range, which is chain data but still an operational artefact
# of a particular run — and on a busy range a single log is megabytes. Keep
# them, archive them, just do not commit them by accident.
/scans/
scan-*.json
.scan-*.tmp

# Recipient lists written by -out.
recipients.txt
addresses.txt

# Build output.
zts-airdrop
zts-airdrop.exe
/dist/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.test

# Go workspace files, which pin local paths that are not portable.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editors and OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
